WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:05.870
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, yesterday in
my episode 4 review I asked you to submit

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:10.430
all of your questions about all the big changes
to the books and the big reveal at the end.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:14.090
So I picked 10 of them to answer in this video
with one bonus question.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.420
Real quick though, congratulations to Noah
Lieberman.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.030
You’re the winner of the giveaway this week.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.450
I’ll be dm’ing you on your channel for
details.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.950
The next round will start when I post my episode
5 review.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.720
If you’re just now finding me every week
for my bigger videos like Game of Thrones,

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.230
Arrow or Doctor Who I post Q&amp;A bonus videos
where I answer you guys directly in a video.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.430
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:40.990
It’s just a fun way to dig a little deeper
on something when they do crazy stuff like

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:41.990
they did last night.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:42.990
So let’s answer some questions.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.850
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.850
Here we go.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.930
Question 1 - Blake Targaryen asks where are
the dragons kept when we’re not seeing them

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.770
next to Daenerys?

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.380
They basically hunt for themselves at this
point.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.920
So instead of riding around in those crates
like they did when they were little they fly

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.680
free all the time.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.049
So if they’re not right there with her,
just assume they’re killing large animals.

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:08.020
They’ll be back soon, there are a few shots
in the trailers that haven’t happened yet.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.549
They just save money for other CG shots by
not using them in every episode.

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:14.100
I actually really like the designs of them
this season.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.840
George RR Martin even posted some artwork
for a full size Balerion that’s going to

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.600
be in the new World of Ice and Fire book this
winter.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.990
Look at the scale.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:25.999
That’s probably how big Drogon is going
to get.

00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:31.220
Question 2 - Chris Todd asks if Locke takes
the Night’s Watch Oath and ends up completing

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.609
his mission to kill Bran and Jon Snow and
then returns to Bolton, wouldn’t he be branded

00:01:35.609 --> 00:01:38.329
a deserter and sentenced to death?

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:45.240
Yes totally, but that’s assuming that Roose
Bolton upholds the law and he looks like he

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.920
doesn’t care about justice.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.090
So if Locke were to be successful in his mission
and head back to Bolton, the only way he’d

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.380
face the chopping block like the brother Ned
Stark beheaded in season 1,is if one of the

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.270
more honorable houses caught him.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.499
Right now I’m going to say that there aren’t
a whole lot of those in power.

00:02:00.499 --> 00:02:03.840
And the only way you’d know someone was
a brother of the Night’s Watch is if he

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.799
told you or he was wearing the Black.

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:08.700
So all Locke has to do is change clothes.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.140
I don’t think he’s going to be successful
though.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:19.879
I think either Bran or Jon Snow or hopefully
a White Walker will kill him.

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:24.260
Question 3 - Raquel Braga asks what’s the
difference between White Walkers and the blue

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.599
eyed people that come back from the dead?

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:33.250
The White Walkers are living beings and the
undead people, called wights, are re-animated

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.320
corpses.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.180
The White Walkers practice necromancy, so
they find dead bodies or they kill people,

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.849
then turn them into zombies that obey their
commands.

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:47.989
Even though we watched that baby get turned
into a White Walker, we still haven’t seen

00:02:47.989 --> 00:02:49.950
a White Walker raise someone from the dead.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.349
I’m sure the show will do that in an episode
eventually.

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:56.459
Question 4 - Soraya asks Are you happy about
all the changes and how they are changing

00:02:56.459 --> 00:02:57.469
character's arcs?﻿

00:02:57.469 --> 00:03:01.500
I think it’s a little strange but I don’t
mind.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.549
They’re still good storytellers.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:07.969
The interesting thing we should be talking
about is how these changes are going to affect

00:03:07.969 --> 00:03:10.050
what happens way way later ni the story.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:15.250
George RR Martin was using the term Butterfly
Effect to describe what was happening with

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.250
the show.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:22.829
They kill or don’t kill a certain character
in season 1 or bring a new character on and

00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:27.049
it means they have to change the story later
to accomodate things.

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:31.569
He was basically setting us up for a time
when the show becomes unrecognizable from

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:32.569
the books.

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:35.959
But they still operate based on the original
character arcs.

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:39.739
So even though the order of events might change
or where characters physically travel, like

00:03:39.739 --> 00:03:41.470
Bran being at Craster’s now.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.499
Their character development will stay the
same.

00:03:43.499 --> 00:03:46.140
Like all of the mega major events will still
be the same.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:54.409
It’s just the way characters get there that’s
changing.

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:56.760
In the case of that end moment with the White
Walkers too.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.930
That’s something that was probably going
on during Book 2 and 3, but Martin just never

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:01.930
wrote in.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.920
So chronologically they didn’t spoil Winds
of Winter or anything.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.069
They just chose to show us a part of Westeros
that Martin didn’t focus on.

00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:12.879
So they could always end up doing the same
thing for other characters and places too.

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:16.530
Be prepared for that.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.530
Question 5 - Trafalgar Law asks Do you think
that one of the white walkers seen in this

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.320
episode was Coldhands?﻿

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.480
No, the White Walker with the horns on his
head or crown was the Night’s King.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:31.090
In the mythology of the books he was the 13th
Lord Commander of the Night’s Watch.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:36.200
That was like 8,000 years ago, close to the
time when the Wall was first built.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.630
After the last great battle with the White
Walkers.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:43.090
The story goes that he was out on patrol North
of The Wall and met a woman who looked kind

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.650
of like the bride of Frankenstein and fell
in love with her.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:50.840
When he had sex with her he supposedly lost
his soul and looked like we saw him on the

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:51.840
show.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.431
It implies that by giving himself to her he
lost his soul and she turned him into a white

00:04:55.431 --> 00:04:56.431
walker.

00:04:56.431 --> 00:05:01.510
Then he went on to enslave a giant portion
of the Night’s Watch brothers and a war

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:02.510
started.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:06.510
Eventually he was defeated and no one ever
heard from him again.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:10.060
But since that person we just saw was him,
it looks like he just retreated and created

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:13.740
a new center of power for the Great Other
in the frozen north.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.080
Slowly creating more acolytes, White Walkers,
from sacrifices to the Great Other by people

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.350
like Craster living in the North

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:23.370
If you look in the background too there’s
some visual clues that give him away as the

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.370
Night’s King.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:29.040
It seems like the writers put 12 other white
walkers behind him to represent the other

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.590
12 Lord Commanders that came before him.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.940
Obviously he only became Lord Commander after
they died.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.550
So it’s just an easter egg.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.100
Those people behind him aren’t his predecessors.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:42.180
Question 6 - Effective Kill asks If white
walkers are made from babies, where did the

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:44.650
first white walkers come from?

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.160
So we don’t really know anything about the
Long Night, that was the first war with the

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.310
Great Other.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.250
After that ended Brandon Stark built the wall.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.470
That’s why he’s called Bran the builder.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:55.560
Like I said, that was about 8,000 years ago.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.090
But it seems like the Night’s King became
the first new White Walker after that.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.440
If he really is a White Walker and not something
different.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.440
He’s a servant of the Great Other, like
the King of their people now.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.380
It’s also possible that the Night’s Queen
was the first new one, and she turned him.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.900
Because he was human until she took his soul.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:12.830
We don’t know a lot about her yet either.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:15.220
Hopefully the new books will fill in the gaps.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.980
As for all the new White Walkers we see on
the show, it looks like the reason it’s

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:24.190
taking them so long to build their army back
up is because they’re dependent on sacrificial

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.190
babies.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:28.270
It seems like anyone who worships the Great
Other sacrifices their male sons.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:30.650
But not everyone in the North worships him.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:34.250
The wildlings mostly worship the gods of the
forest.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:39.410
Right now we don’t know how many white walkers
actually exist, but that baby we saw was supposedly

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.220
his 99th son.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:44.350
So there’s at least 100 white walkers if
you include the Night’s King.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:48.690
They all practice magic, so it would be like
100 Melisandre’s.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:51.600
But some of them obviously are more warriors
and some magic users.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:56.850
Question 7 - Lizzie asks What was the point
of Carl drinking wine from Jeor Mormont's

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.850
skull?

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:01.160
I think they’re just trying to make Burn
Gorman’s character seem every bit as evil

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:04.500
as the White Walkers and Ramsay Snow.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.490
Like just as evil as the other evil characters
on the show.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:12.160
Remember Daenerys’ speech answering Injustice
with Justice.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.270
Karl is injustice.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:18.680
I think they let him go a little bit crazy
over the top just because they liked his performance.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:22.940
Burn Gorman is great and there was a real
shakespearean flair he had when he was talking

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:23.940
to the skull.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:26.550
I feel like that’s a scene all the theater
geeks would really enjoy.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.350
You could perform that as a one-person scene
at school.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:33.230
In fact, I will totally give a shout out to
anyone who wants to try and recreate that

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.690
scene either at home or in front of people.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:38.430
Starting from his first line up to the point
he starts kicking people and puts the skull

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.430
down.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.240
Question 8 - Illyas (no avatar) asks Do you
think Tommen will stay good or will he also

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.330
become as evil as Joffrey?﻿

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.890
I think it’s implied that he has a good
heart and if he survives to adulthood, he

00:07:47.890 --> 00:07:52.510
won’t have the same madness that Joffrey
had and that King Aerys developed.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:56.390
Remember Cersei said that when Joffrey was
little he was totally normal, he only started

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:58.560
to go mad as he got older.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.970
And Barristan Selmy said the same thing about
King Aerys, Daenerys’ father.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:06.370
He was normal too until he slowly turned into
the Mad King.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:08.300
I always thought that madness was a result
of all the inbreeding, like George RR Martin

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:18.190
was implying that by doing something so taboo,
the Targaryens and Cersei and Jaime were being

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.360
punished by the gods.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:24.740
In reality, it’s probably some genetic anomaly
having to do with inbreeding, in fact, I was

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:29.540
always amazed that the Targaryens didn’t
have more birth defects or quote unquote crazy

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:30.540
Kings.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:34.970
Supposedly sisterwiving was a totally acceptable
thing to do in ancient Valyria.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:40.520
But they mostly did it to keep the dragon-rider
blood magic as strong as possible.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.320
Being a dragon rider was something that was
transmitted genetically.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:48.690
Question 9 - nicnacz asks how are the story
changes going to influence Bran's storyline?

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.880
I still think he’s going to travel to meet
the three-eyed raven eventually.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.160
He’s just on something of a temporary detour.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:00.360
The finale is titled The Children, so I think
the Children of the Forest will get involved

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:02.100
somehow and help him.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.260
They also have the greensight like Bran.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:08.610
So anytime they pop up it will probably be
as part of Bran’s storyline.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:12.610
No confirmation on when we’ll see them for
the first time though.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:17.150
Question 10 - Avi asks, what’s the difference
between the Great Other, the person we saw

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.740
at the end and the white walkers?

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:23.740
So the Great Other is the diametric opposite
to the Red God.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:28.850
They’re like a yin and yang supernatural
force and they always exist in relationship

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:31.080
to each other.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.090
So when one is in power, the other is not.

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:37.181
Like the way people mythologize the Sun and
the Moon.

00:09:37.181 --> 00:09:41.770
I suppose the show is making it seem like
the Red God is a force for good or light as

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:44.150
Melisandre says, and the Great Other is evil.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.420
But I like to think of them as being relatively
neutral.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:50.940
Like the Red God isn’t a warm fuzzy god,
and we don’t really know what the Great

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:51.940
Other wants yet.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:55.950
So The Great Other is the unseen supernatural
force, the person we saw is the Night’s

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.390
King, think of him as like the leader of the
White Walkers, the other White Walkers are

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.410
just normal soldiers.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.390
They all possess a certain level of magical
abilities though.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:06.210
The one we saw just seems more powerful.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:10.950
and one last Bonus Question - Arman (no avatar)
asks When are we going to learn more about

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.760
the land of forever winter?

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:17.460
We’re not going to see that place until
Winds of Winter.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:21.529
The Ice Fortress we saw at the end of the
episode is at some indeterminate location

00:10:21.529 --> 00:10:22.529
in the North.

00:10:22.529 --> 00:10:23.529
It could be anywhere.

00:10:23.529 --> 00:10:25.310
They don’t specifically say where.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:28.460
So thank you so much for submitting questions,
these are always fun to do.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.770
Especially when crazy stuff happens in the
episode.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:34.930
Because we got a mega white walker scene at
the end I think my next bonus video will be

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:42.900
about the Long Night, that last war with the
white walkers and the building of the Wall.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.320
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:49.740
And feel free to leave me suggestions for
future bonus videos.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:53.270
Right now click here for my review of the
episode and click here to learn all about

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:54.270
the Bloodraven.

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.880
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:56.010
High Fives!

